 "prompt": "This 2x2 flush floor hatch is broken: it does not do what it should. Repair it.\n\nGoal: A 2x2 hatch (0..1, 0, 0..1) in the smooth-stone floor: closed (four stone blocks, flush with the floor) while the lever is off, open (all four cells empty) while it is on. The smooth-stone floor ring must never move.\n\nSpec (checked in the game engine):\n- Lever at [2, -5, 0]; it starts off. The grader settles the build, then flips the lever 6 times (idle gaps [0, 3, 7, 1, 11, 2] ticks before each flip).\n- After each flip the build must come to rest within 60 ticks, then stay unchanged for 40 ticks.\n- Lever off (start and after every even flip): (0..1, 0, 0..1) is stone.\n- Lever on (after every odd flip): (0..1, 0, 0..1) is air.\n- The whole build must return to exactly the same resting state every two flips; no item drops; no block may leave the box.\n- At most 28 blocks (lever included), all inside the box [-2, -6, -2]..[3, 1, 3].\n- These cells must stay empty at every tick: [[[0, 1], [1, 2], [0, 1]]].\n- 12 fixed cells must keep their block at every tick: [-1, 0, -1], [-1, 0, 0], [-1, 0, 1], [-1, 0, 2], [0, 0, -1], [0, 0, 2], [1, 0, -1], [1, 0, 2], [2, 0, -1], [2, 0, 0], [2, 0, 1], [2, 0, 2].\n\nYou may change, add or remove any blocks except the lever. Allowed blocks: the benchmark allow-list. Submit the complete build as a list of blocks.",
 "verified": true
}